Um... I'm not sure (at 3 am, I'm *never* sure :)  but it looks to me like the
question was "can I save a game, then start a different (new) game such that
the game I saved doesn't start up?"

If that's the case, the answer is yes.  Just play using a different name (you
can do this either by setting the NETHACKOPTIONS environment variable or by
invoking nethack with the -u option (i.e. nethack -u MolassesBrain)

If that's not the case, than the above should be treated as what they are: the
mindless ramblings of someone who's spent the last 5 hours munging their way
around the nethack source code trying to figure out what all those strange
little attributes do... 

Exciting way to spend your Saturday night, no? :)

